// cobc: the code generator written in CobaltC (D-0274), the self-hosting
// compiler's back end over the front end of impl/front.
//
//   cobc --emit-c [--c-name NAME] [-o OUT] FILE
//
// writes the program's C to OUT, or prints it on standard output without `-o`
// or with `-o -`; NAME is the C file's name, which its `#line` directives
// name (default OUT, else a.c). A program the static pass rejects gets its
// diagnostic, and status 1, and OUT is not written.
//
// Any other command line is the driver's (`driver.cb`): its options,
// messages, exit statuses, files and commands.

